# Reference walk for the chapter-skip spread check. One instance, no peer, so a press turns exactly
# one page and a long press skips exactly one chapter -- which makes this the ground truth the pair
# is measured against.
#
# It performs the same long press the left half performs, so shot 00 is the chapter's first page and
# shot 01 is its second. A spread reader that skipped correctly shows 00 on the left and 01 on the
# right.
#
# Its settings file is the left half's, byte for byte, so nothing that depends on a setting can
# differ between this walk and the run it measures. Only peer presence differs, which is the point.
log pageflip-skip-solo: start
expect_timeout 90000
expect Entering activity: Home
wait 800
tap confirm
expect Entering activity: EpubReader
# First open builds the first chapter's cache.
wait 9000
# The control shot: this walk and the left half both sit at spine 0 page 0 here, with the same
# settings file, differing only in whether a peer is present. It is the only comparison that can
# say whether peer presence is in the pixels, which decides whether a solo walk can ever be a
# byte-exact reference for a paired half.
screenshot /screenshots/pf-sk-solo-ctl.bmp
# The chapter skip: held past SKIP_HOLD_MS (700 ms), which suppresses the release that follows.
press down
wait 900
release down
# The chapter this lands in has never been laid out, so this wait is a cold build. It has to be
# long enough for the build to finish and not merely to have started: a press that arrives while
# the section is still settling is swallowed, and the second shot then duplicates the first.
wait 14000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-sk-solo-00.bmp
tap down
wait 5000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-sk-solo-01.bmp
log pageflip-skip-solo: done
quit
